4 Concluding Observations 


I started this paper with the observation that the term Atimarga, although 
certainly useful for referring to the ascetic strand of early Saivism, appears 
not to have been used by “Atimargins” themselves. The term represents, by all 
accounts, a Mantramargic perspective on the formation of the Saiva religion.3? 

The Varanasimahatmya discussed in this paper is the only exception that I 
know of in which we do find the term Atimarga—as well as the related term 
Lokatita—used outside of a Mantramargic context. Several observations can 
be made with reference to the passages of the Varanasimahatmya discussed 
here: 


