played an important role in popularizing tantric Saivism at an early stage is 
suggested by the fact that the Mrgendra extends the scope of the lokadharmint 
dīksā to those who are not even Šiva-worshippers, people who may nonetheless 
have desired specific services distinctive to the Saiva tantric domain. However, 
the doctrinally awkward position of the lokadharmi Sādhaka, combined with 
the increasing emphasis on purely soteriological goals, may have led to the 
gradual oblivion of this category, causing its reassignment in later sources, as 
will be seen below. 


