Nagabhata 11 is called paramabhagavatībhakta.!” It may be a coincidence, but 
the latter's mother is named Sundari. In any case, this Vatsaraja could be our 
poet.! Our text represents an archaic tradition that does not even know the 
name Tripurasundari, and thus this date in the early-ninth century CE fits it 
well. 


