ask, under what conditions may satya be taken as "Pure or Sacred”? Satya could 
no longer be accepted as "True to life" as interpreted by Kramrisch (1928, 51). 
Another term, which intensified this problem, was sadrgya, which could not be 
allowed to retain its usual sense (Coomaraswamy 1933, 21): 


If we understood sādršya then to mean “illusion” or “realism,” verisimil- 
